{"id":898,"slug":"the-love-parade","title":"The Love Parade","year":1929,"country":"United States","duration":107,"spine":null,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/898-the-love-parade","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/092ac9cf0eaa4c11e76d0d2570423e31/Y5aPGnRmedNsiC4EeiQP9WUe9WrNY7_large.jpg","description":"Ernst Lubitsch’s first full talkie was also Hollywood’s first movie musical to integrate songs with narrative. Additionally, The Love Parade made stars out of toast-of-Paris Maurice Chevalier and girl-from-Philly Jeanette MacDonald, cast as a womanizing military attaché and the man-hungry queen of “Sylvania,” respectively. With its naughty innuendo and satiric romance, The Love Parade opened the door for a decade of witty screen battles of the sexes.The Love Parade was restored in 4K resolution by Universal Pictures in collaboration with The Film Foundation.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Ernst Lubitsch","slug":"ernst-lubitsch"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Maurice Chevalier","role":"Count Alfred Renard","slug":"maurice-chevalier"},{"actor":"Jeanette MacDonald","role":"Queen Louise","slug":"jeanette-macdonald"},{"actor":"Lupino Lane","role":"Jacques","slug":"lupino-lane"},{"actor":"Lillian Roth","role":"Lulu","slug":"lillian-roth"},{"actor":"Eugene Pallette","role":"War Minister","slug":"eugene-pallette"},{"actor":"E. H. Calvert","role":"Ambassador","slug":"e-h-calvert"},{"actor":"Edgar Norton","role":"Master of Ceremonies","slug":"edgar-norton"},{"actor":"Lionel Belmore","role":"Prime Minister","slug":"lionel-belmore"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Ernst Lubitsch","slug":"ernst-lubitsch"},{"role":"Producer","person":"Ernst Lubitsch","slug":"ernst-lubitsch"},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Ernest Vajda","slug":null},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Guy Bolton","slug":null},{"role":"From the play by","person":"Leon Xanrof","slug":null},{"role":"Cinematography","person":"Victor Milner","slug":null},{"role":"Editor","person"